# Nivo78 Rule Projection — 19-operating-model-release-certification

**Binding status:** This file is a maintained enforcement projection of the canonical Nivo78 Product Standard.
**Source:** `reference/NIVO78_APP_STANDARD.txt`
**Authority:** The canonical standard and rule-ID catalog control if this projection and the source ever differ.

## Agent instructions
- Apply this rule whenever the work described by the rule is relevant.
- Treat every requirement below as binding unless the canonical standard marks it as `[QA]`/conditional or an approved override applies.
- Preserve and mention canonical `APP-*`, `WEB-*`, `MARKETING-*`, and other rule IDs when reporting compliance or exceptions.
- Do not weaken a requirement merely because it is inconvenient to implement.
- If a requirement cannot be met, stop before shipping and use the standard override process.

---

MAKING THIS A STANDARD TO LIVE BY

\================================================================================



1\. Canonical document (this file)

   - Version
with a short changelog when rules change; products declare compliance in
release notes only when the standard changes affect ship criteria.



2\. Binding agent and developer rules

   - Mirror the
focused standard projections under .cursor/rules/ so AI and humans get the
same bar. The canonical standard remains in N78Ops.

   - New
products copy the rule set on day one — no renegotiation per app.



3\. Shared libraries (implementation spine)

   -
nivo78-theme: visual components and tokens — no duplicate buttons or fields in
product repos.

   -
nivo78-breadcrumbs: debug-only 10,000-event ring buffer; expect/actual
isDebugBuild + MutexLock;

     export
utility in androidDebug/debug source sets only (APP-BREADCRUMB-DEBUG-ONLY).

   -
nivo78-support (recommended shared module): Feedback page contract, diagnostics
snapshot builder, privacy redactor, mailto composer, support URL registry —
products inject product-specific snapshot fields only.

   - Engine
packages own validation, help article ids, and export naming — UI wires, does
not reinvent.



4\. New product checklist

   -
reference/NIVO78\_NEW\_PRODUCT\_CHECKLIST.txt — run before first public build.



5\. Release gate extensions

   - Support
menu destinations registered; Feedback diagnostics redactor unit tests; legal
URLs in support URL registry.

   - Text tests:
grep user strings for banned jargon, “coming soon,” and implied automation;
verify ? help on new non-trivial fields.



6\. Cross-product review

   - When
shipping a UI change in one app, ask: “Should this move to nivo78-theme or
nivo78-support?”

   - Quarterly
pass: open shipped Nivo78 apps side by side — menu labels, Feedback flow, field
error placement, save bar — fix drift in the shared layer first.



7\. Help and website sync (updocs)

   - Privacy,
Terms, Support HTML, and Help KB stay aligned with shipped app behavior.

   - Feedback
intro and support page state the same data-on-device story as the privacy page.

   - Run
tools/maintain/run-updocs.ps1 after security, legal, or help copy changes.



8\. Website verify in release gate

   - Required
in-repo pages under code/Website/{product}/; verify script checks files and
standard content markers.

   - WEB SEO
checks (meta description, canonical, Open Graph, Twitter; hosted n78\_seo\_head.php
when sibling Website repo present) run with WEB standard checks — failures
block release unless overridden.

   - Store
listing privacy/terms URLs must equal in-app and in-repo paths.



9\. Training heuristic for designers and contributors

   - “Would a
user of another Nivo78 app know where to click without relearning?”

   - If no, fix
chrome or naming in the shared standard — not a one-off in a single product.



10\. Compliance statement per release (internal)

   - Short
checklist in release gate log: engine/UI separation, offline core path,
Feedback diagnostics opt-in, legal links, website verify green (WEB standard +
WEB SEO), regression green.





\================================================================================

PRE-SHIP BAR (EXTENDED — FAMILY CONSISTENCY)

\================================================================================



\- Shared theme components used for all primary inputs
and buttons; no one-off form controls on critical paths.

\- Structured fields format and validate on blur / Done
/ leave / Save only — not on every keystroke (APP-INPUT-FORMAT-ON-COMMIT).

\- Blur-only drafts flush before Save / Lock / Next /
Finish / leave (APP-INPUT-FLUSH-BEFORE-PERSIST).

  Persist from
inner committed text; live editor state after flush — not a leftover parent
copy or

  leftover
composed snapshot.

\- Text fields focus for in-place edit — never
select-all or clear on focus (APP-INPUT-FOCUS-EDIT-ONLY).

\- Save inactive vs last registry-verified values;
persist valid on leave, block invalid leave (APP-SAVE-VERIFIED-INACTIVE,
APP-LEAVE-DIRTY-PROMPT).

\- Accessibility floor on mobile (APP-UI-A11Y-FLOOR).

\- Help, Feedback, Support center, Privacy, Terms
reachable from main chrome without completing a workflow.

\- Feedback page matches report types, contact fields,
mailto handoff, **APP-FEEDBACK-BUG-NARRATIVE** email section headers (doing /
happened / expected, --- SETTINGS_FOR_SUPPORT ---), diagnostics checkbox
contract, and device-vs-web routing (bugs in-app only; no extended diagnostics
on feature requests).

\- Diagnostics snapshot built in engine/support layer
with redaction tests; no PII or secrets in default payload.

\- Debug-only breadcrumb ring buffer present;
debug-only breadcrumb verification green; export not in main/release.

\- Privacy and Terms URLs registered in one support URL
object; same URLs linked from menu and Feedback footer.

\- Export and copy actions use plain labels and
consistent success/error feedback.

\- Cross-check against another shipped Nivo78 app for
menu order, save bar placement, and field error pattern — document intentional
differences only.

\- Web: code/Website/{product}/ pages present; legal.css
shared template; support/privacy/terms copy aligned with app; product index
will/won’t sections; comprehensive SEO on every public page;
verify-apa-website.ps1 green including WEB SEO checks.

\- Legal gate: consent dialog, decline integrity,
versioned acceptance, re-consent on terms bump; Legal.txt green when legal
surfaces change.

\- Trust: destructive confirms, vault/recovery
warnings, schema migration tests, backup/restore path documented.





\================================================================================

RELEASE CERTIFICATION (FINAL GATE CHECKLIST)

\================================================================================



Use as the final release gate. Compact checklist for
existing verify / release-gate tooling.

A product is not release-ready until every applicable
item is checked or covered by an approved override.



[ ] Build succeeds from the approved source state.

[ ] Static N78 rules pass.

[ ] Required automated tests pass.

[ ] Critical recovery and migration tests pass.

[ ] Security / dependency checks pass.

[ ] Release contains no development-only bypasses or
credentials.

[ ] Accessibility floor has been verified.

[ ] Offline behavior has been verified for
offline-capable workflows.

[ ] Backup / export / restore behavior has been
verified where applicable.

[ ] Version and release metadata are consistent.

[ ] Required Help, Privacy, Terms, and release
documentation are present.

[ ] Active overrides have been reviewed.

[ ] The exact release artifact has been verified and approved.



Rule ids: APP-RELEASE-DEFINITION-OF-DONE,
APP-RELEASE-ARTIFACT-INTEGRITY, APP-TEST-REGRESSION,

APP-SEC-RELEASE-DEBUG, APP-RELEASE-DEBUG-CLEAN, and
related APP-TEST-\*, APP-BACKUP-\*, APP-A11Y-\*,

APP-OVERRIDE-REVIEW.

